{
  "note": "Canonical weekly sweep behavior (GSD parity decision D-14; spec gsd-taskmanager/tasks/spec-weekly-sweep.md). The web repo is the authority: gsd-taskmanager/tests/fixtures/cross-platform/sweep-corpus.json. Byte-identical copies belong at gsd-iosapp/GSDKit/Tests/GSDModelTests/Fixtures/sweep-corpus.json and gsd-android/core/model/src/test/resources/fixtures/cross-platform/sweep-corpus.json, and every suite runs every case. A task field left out takes the model's default: not urgent, not important, not completed, savedAt and dueDate null, createdAt and updatedAt 2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z, location active. location isn't a task field: the test keeps only active rows before calling the function, because archived and trashed rows live in their own stores. windowDays null means escalation is Off, and escalation itself is pinned by escalation-corpus.json. Every age is a count of local calendar days in zone, never elapsed time. reminder.weekday is ISO: 1 is Monday and 7 is Sunday. A local time inside a daylight-saving gap shifts forward by the length of the gap, and a time inside an overlap takes the first occurrence. If behavior changes, change the spec, this file in all three repos, and all three implementations together.",
